WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.860
When the sun rose on that fateful day, Jerry
Marks had been one of the lucky ones.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.920
He worked in a mine, deep underground, at
the edge of a small town in the rural United

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.920
States.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.170
Which meant he didn’t see what happened
when day broke, when the light of the sun

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.750
ravaged the Earth.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:23.740
The first Jerry heard about it was when his
son Kyle came racing into the mine, frantically

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.570
tapping his dad’s shoulder to get his attention.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:31.769
He’d run all the way from their tiny homestead
under a fireproof blanket, thick and long

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:36.050
enough to block the sunlight from touching
any part of Kyle’s skin.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.539
His older sister, Jerry’s daughter Carly,
hadn’t been so lucky.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:46.100
Caught by the light, her body had turned the
consistency of warm candle wax, melting into

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.469
a form that barely resembled human anymore.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:54.000
Jerry had been one of a handful of others
working late in the mine that day.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.970
A few thought that young Kyle had made the
whole story up, and ventured up to the surface

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:02.900
– and into the light – only to meet the
same, twisted fate.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:09.150
The light morphed their bodies into monstrosities,
anyone in the small, rural community becoming

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.930
an amorphous mass of human flesh.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:17.270
Eventually, those that stayed behind in the
mine heard the voices of their loved ones,

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:22.850
their wives, husbands, children, all calling
out to them from outside.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:28.080
They promised that nothing was wrong, that
it was a lovely, sunny day outside, and the

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.540
mine workers should clock out to come and
enjoy it.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:36.009
More of them left, reassured by hearing their
families that all was well.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:40.000
And once more, none of them were seen again.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.640
Only Jerry and Kyle were left, and it stayed
that way for several months.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.680
The father and son had to adapt to life underground,
only leaving the mine to forage for food – and

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.080
only while wearing thick, dirty mining overalls,
making sure not a single millimeter of skin

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.210
was on display.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.899
If the sunlight touched them, they’d never
make it back alive.

00:02:01.899 --> 00:02:06.000
Venturing out of the mine in his overalls,
Jerry had seen the shuffling, melted mass

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.360
that had once been the townsfolk.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:13.310
He did his best to avoid it as he went house
to house, making sure it never saw him while

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:16.080
he raided cupboards and refrigerators.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.510
But he could see it, and among the blobs of
bodies blended together, he saw something

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.060
that resembled his daughter.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.739
It turned his stomach, not just knowing but
actually witnessing what had happened to her.

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:33.330
And it was made all the worse on the days
that Carly called out to him and Kyle, while

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.019
they hid in the mine.

00:02:35.019 --> 00:02:40.420
It was clearly her voice, but there was something
wrong about it; perhaps knowing that she was

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:46.950
a part of the melted monstrosity made it easier
to resist her trying to coax them out into

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:47.950
the light.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:52.540
It had been almost an entire year of life
spent mostly underground when Jerry and Kyle

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:57.990
encountered their first actual human beings
since all the other workers had left the mine.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:03.050
The pair that arrived were strange, wearing
protective suits that covered them both head

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.330
to toe.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.349
Just like Jerry and Kyle had quickly realised,
these two were aware that not even the tiniest

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:13.360
hint of the sun’s unforgiving light could
be allowed to reach them.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.860
The two approached Jerry and Kyle seemingly
coming in peace, although the father and son

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.569
remained cautious of the newcomers.

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:25.030
Making sure they were deep enough in the mine
to avoid the sunlight at the stony entrance,

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:30.680
the pair of them revealed their faces, confirming
they were still fully human, before introducing

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:36.379
themselves as Researcher Worth and Sergeant
Booker of the SCP Foundation.

00:03:36.379 --> 00:03:40.549
Sitting down with Jerry, Worth explained to
him what had really happened; he had been

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:45.319
working for an organization that contained
and studied anomalous creatures and phenomena,

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:46.480
the Foundation.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.959
Booker had been a member of a special armed
unit within the same establishment, or a Mobile

00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:52.959
Task Force.

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:58.459
But now the SCP Foundation itself had fallen,
with a number of its own personnel turned

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:01.840
into more of the amorphous fleshy creatures
in the sunlight.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.900
“We spent a lot of years keeping all this
from the public,” Worth admitted, sounding

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.579
guilty but implying the choice was out of
his hands.

00:04:08.579 --> 00:04:11.340
“But I don’t suppose there’s any point
in secrets anymore.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.410
It’s the sun, you see, Mr Marks-”
“You can call me Jerry,” he interrupted.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.030
“Sorry, Jerry,” Worth corrected himself.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.930
“But something happened to the sun.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:25.570
It changed, decimated the entire planet in
barely any time at all.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.700
I mean all those people, millions… billions
all at once.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.700
Dear god.”

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:34.910
Worth took a moment as the existential dread
of it all once again caught up with him.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.400
“It turned out the biggest anomaly was right
above us,” Booker continued for him; she

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.449
sounded a lot more stoic, even a little coldly
detached from it all.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:47.010
“SCP-001, that’s what the Foundation called
it.”

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.190
“Is there a way to reverse it?

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.730
Or cure the people that the sunlight…

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:52.850
changes?”

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.759
Jerry asked, thinking of Carly.

00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:55.880
“You mean SCP-001-A?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:02.419
No, I’m sorry, Jerry, there’s nothing
we can do,” the researcher said, failing

00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:05.270
to sound as recomposed as he pretended to
be.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.470
“Your daughter is gone, but at least you
still have your-”

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.350
Worth paused, looking around the mine.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:14.050
Even in the low light, there was no sign of
Kyle.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:18.729
Jerry turned to scan the area; to his horror,
his son seemed to have vanished while they

00:05:18.729 --> 00:05:19.729
were talking.

00:05:19.729 --> 00:05:23.080
Instantly, panic caused him to think that
Kyle had wandered out of the mine and into

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:29.330
the sunlight, turning into part of what Worth
had called SCP-001-A. But the boy would’ve

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.660
had to walk past Jerry to start heading that
direction, plus the father knew his son was

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:38.639
far too scared to go outside after seeing
what the sun had done to Carly.

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:43.610
Booker had a tactical bag filled with equipment,
flashlights, spare batteries, even flares

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.889
for when the power in those ran out.

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:50.020
And both working and living in the mine so
long, Jerry had maps, knew certain routes

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.870
through the deep network of tunnels almost
by heart.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.530
Between them, the three had enough to mount
a search for the missing Kyle.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.620
Keeping together, they traversed away from
the first of several larger chambers, down

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.789
into the dark depths of the mine.

00:06:02.789 --> 00:06:05.960
“Kyle!” his father yelled, his voice echoing
through the tunnel.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.960
“Kyle, buddy, it’s dad!

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:08.970
You there?”

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:13.740
Walking behind him, Researcher Worth and Sergeant
Booker parroted the calls, assuring the missing

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.840
boy that they didn’t mean him or Jerry any
harm.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.860
As the trio walked deeper and deeper, they
began to venture into a portion of the mine

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.009
that had hardly been used by the workers.

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:28.080
It was darker than the areas further up; while
those had rows of electric lamps powered by

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.460
long cables attached to generators, down here
the only light came from the flashlights the

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.470
group carried.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.160
“Kyle, come on out!”

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.349
Jerry called out for his son again.

00:06:38.349 --> 00:06:41.139
“This isn’t the time to split up, we need
to stick together!

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:43.380
Come on son, I’m really worried here!”

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.540
Once again, there was no answer.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:49.560
Just then, Jerry caught sight of Booker and
Worth out of the corner of his eye.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:54.350
Both of them knew a lot about SCP-001, and
the mine worker couldn’t help the suspicion

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.000
that added to his perception of them.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.310
After all, Kyle had never run off before now,
and Jerry couldn’t help but think, while

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:06.300
his attention had been turned, that the pair
of Foundation personnel had taken his son.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.580
“Dad?” a voice suddenly called out.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.190
Jerry’s head spun on a swivel at the sound
of Kyle calling for him.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.629
“Dad, where are you?”

00:07:13.629 --> 00:07:15.220
it echoed through the tunnel again.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.220
“That’s him!”

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.629
Jerry exclaimed to the other two.

00:07:17.629 --> 00:07:19.000
“Which way did that come from?”

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.479
“Straight ahead, it sounds like,” Booker
replied.

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:23.220
“Hold on,” Worth interjected.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.280
“I think you two should look at this.”

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:29.110
The beam from his flashlight was pointed at
the rocky floor of the tunnel.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:34.860
Something was gleaming, wet against the stone:
a large smear of red, like something had been

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.770
dragged in the direction Kyle’s voice was
coming from.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.319
“Oh god, he could be hurt!”

00:07:39.319 --> 00:07:40.729
Jerry said urgently.

00:07:40.729 --> 00:07:45.099
“Hurt might not be the right word, I’m
afraid, Jerry,” the researcher said solemnly.

00:07:45.099 --> 00:07:46.930
“There’s a lot of blood here.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:47.930
Too much.”

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.580
“All the more reason to go further and find
where he’s calling from,” the father retorted

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:52.580
angrily.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:58.270
“That’s if it is actually the kid calling
us,” Booker replied, her and Worth exchanging

00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.840
a worried glance at each other.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.639
“You two know something, don’t you?”

00:08:01.639 --> 00:08:02.639
Jerry demanded.

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:06.290
“Does that… the thing from outside, does
it have my son too?”

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.349
“Dad?” another voice called.

00:08:08.349 --> 00:08:12.340
Jerry froze, his blood as cold as the mine
tunnel he was still stood in.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:18.270
He hadn’t heard that voice in almost a year,
but recognised it immediately: it was Carly,

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:19.270
his daughter.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:25.420
It seemed impossible, he knew she had been
merged into part of SCP-001-A when day broke,

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:28.909
but now she was somehow calling out to Jerry.

00:08:28.909 --> 00:08:32.919
Her voice sounded clearer, like it had used
to before she changed.

00:08:32.919 --> 00:08:37.289
And she wasn’t trying to lure her father
out into the sunlight either.

00:08:37.289 --> 00:08:41.349
For a moment, it seemed to Jerry like his
daughter had somehow come back.

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:43.180
“Dad, we’re both over here!”

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.430
Carly’s voice called again.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.240
“We need your help, Kyle’s stuck!”

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.330
“Who is that?”

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.399
Booker whispered.

00:08:48.399 --> 00:08:51.690
“T-that’s Carly,” Jerry sniffed, holding
back tears.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:57.110
“You said your daughter became a part of
SCP-001-A,” Worth pointed out.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:58.730
“Maybe she got better?”

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:59.750
the father asked hopefully.

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:04.350
“I hate to say it, but that’s definitely
not her,” Sergeant Booker replied.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.910
“We should turn back now, if there’s an
anomaly in these tunnels… that’s not gonna

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:11.210
be pretty for any of us,” she added, turning
to Worth.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.210
“What?”

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:13.210
Jerry yelled.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.210
“What do you mean by that?”

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.800
“Look buddy, those aren’t your children,”
the MTF agent said bluntly.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.910
“It sounds like SCP-001-A got them.”

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.320
“No, no, the voices are too clear,” Worth
replied.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.040
“I think there’s something else here.”

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.980
Before Jerry could explode with anger at how
uninterested both Foundation personnel seemed

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:34.630
at the fate of his children, another sound
was heard.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.780
Footsteps, something shuffling closer, padding
its feet on the stone.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:44.370
There was a low growl that filled the tunnel,
as whatever it was came closer still.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:48.600
“Dad?” the voice of Carly repeated, sounding
only a few feet away now.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.910
“Where are you, Dad?”

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.270
Kyle’s voice immediately followed it.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.570
Behind came the sound of Booker striking a
flare.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:59.360
As it erupted into a plume of light and heat,
she threw it down the tunnel: and there they

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.360
were.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:04.340
Not Jerry’s children, but instead a pair
of nightmarish creatures.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:08.420
They backed away from the flare slightly,
but the light still illuminated their blood-red

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:12.170
forms, walking on all fours like wolves.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:17.510
The creature’s elongated heads were missing
any eyes, just jaws filled with rows of sharp,

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.070
red fangs.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:24.030
“Daaaad,” came Kyle’s voice again…
emanating from one of the monsters.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:27.570
It was mimicking Jerry’s son, both his kids.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:33.670
Even having seen SCP-001-A at a distance,
the father could barely believe his eyes.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:34.670
“939s!”

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:37.180
Booker yelled the second her flare illuminated
them.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:38.180
“Run!”

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.620
She pulled a sidearm and opened fire, the
bang of each shot ringing loudly through the

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.620
tunnel.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.390
The pair of SCP-939s pounced at her while
Jerry and Worth turned to run back the way

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.390
they had come.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:52.210
As the creatures attacked, the echoes of gunfire
were replaced with blood-curdling screams.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.220
“What the hell are those things?”

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:56.920
Jerry yelled in a panic.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.920
“SCP-939!”

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:58.920
Researcher Worth panted.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.470
“Too much to explain, they’re pack hunters
and they’re vicious.”

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.050
“What about Kyle and Carly?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.070
I heard their voices!”

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:07.470
“That’s what those monsters do, they mimic
human speech to draw us out.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.470
We’re their prey!

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.350
There’s no telling how long they’ve been
down here, they might have retreated to the

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.170
mine to avoid the sun on the surface!”

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.170
Worth yelled.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.480
The sound of the SCP-939s getting closer were
catching up, right on Jerry’s and Worth’s

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:19.480
heels.

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.140
“What would they come down here for?”

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:24.950
the mine worker huffed, slightly ahead of
the researcher given his slightly stronger

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:25.950
physique.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:26.950
“To escape the sunlight!”

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.930
Worth replied, “SCP-939’s hate bright
li-AAAAAHHHH!”

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:36.490
His sentence was overtaken by a scream as
one of the bloody red creatures caught Worth

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.230
by the ankle, knocking him down and pulling
him back to be devoured.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.870
Jerry didn’t look back, just kept running
back through the tunnel.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:49.070
The sounds of SCP-939 calling after him in
Kyle and Carly’s voices making it even harder

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:51.920
to not stop and turn, even just for a second.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:56.140
But her reminded himself that if he stopped
running, then he couldn’t lure the creatures

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.490
of the mine and into the sunlight…

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:03.900
It wasn’t how he’d ever wanted to go out,
but maybe that way Jerry would see his kids

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:04.900
again.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:10.560
Now go check out “SCP-001 CAN SCP-049 FINALLY
CURE WHEN DAY BREAKS?”

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:17.529
and “SCP-001 WHEN DAY BREAKS SCP-682”
for more horrifying When Day Breaks scenarios!

